const title='DragonSword Awakening Builds — Roles, Runes & Team Order'; const description='DragonSword Awakening builds explained through Hero roles, Karma, Runes, skill priorities, team order and Status/Signal synergy without pretending verified meta builds exist.'; const canonical='https://dragonswordguide.com/builds/'; const article={ '@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'Article',headline:title,description,mainEntityOfPage:canonical,datePublished:'2026-08-08',dateModified:'2026-08-11',publisher:{'@type':'Organization',name:'DragonSword Guide'} }; const sources=[{label:'Official Steam store page',href:sourceUrls.steam,note:'Evidence B — supports 19 Heroes, Status Ailments, Signal Skills and Switching Signals behind this build-planning framework.'}];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} routeId="builds" ogType="article" schema={[article]}><div class="shell page-wrap"><Breadcrumbs items={[{label:'DragonSword Guide',href:'/'},{label:'Builds'}]}/><article><header class="article-header"><p class="eyebrow">Build lab · Evidence-first framework</p><h1>DragonSword Awakening Builds</h1><LastVerified date="August 11, 2026"/></header><QuickAnswer title="A build is a repeatable way to use one Hero inside a three-Hero combat plan."><p>Think through Hero role, combat behavior, Status Ailments, Signal Skills, switching order, Runes, Karma and team context. This is a practical explanation framework based on the official combat loop, not an official eight-part system or a claim that one build is best.</p></QuickAnswer><div class="copy"><h2>What makes a DragonSword Awakening build?</h2><p>A build connects a Hero's identity and resources to the combat sequence around that Hero. The Steam page confirms 19 Heroes with distinct Status Ailment abilities, Active Skills, Signal Skills and Switching Signals; it does not publish a universal build template.</p><ol><li><strong>Hero role:</strong> define what the Hero is trying to contribute in the current encounter.</li><li><strong>Skills and combat behavior:</strong> observe which actions you can execute consistently.</li><li><strong>Status interaction:</strong> identify the condition your sequence is trying to create or exploit.</li><li><strong>Signal Skills:</strong> use the handoff as part of the plan, not as an isolated damage claim.</li><li><strong>Switching order:</strong> test whether the next Hero enters at a useful point in the chain.</li><li><strong>Runes:</strong> treat confirmed capacity and synthesis rules as system facts; do not turn missing stats into a ranking. See the <a href="/systems/runes/">Rune guide</a>.</li><li><strong>Karma:</strong> keep its exact optimization role <span class="evidence-note">NOT_YET_VERIFIED</span> until direct retail data supports a recommendation.</li><li><strong>Team context:</strong> compare a single-Hero plan with the broader <a href="/teams/">team-composition framework</a>.</li></ol><h2>Build vs team composition</h2><p>A <strong>build</strong> is the resources and repeatable play pattern for a Hero within a fight. A <strong>team composition</strong> is the multi-Hero arrangement that creates the conditions, handoffs and payoffs around that Hero. A strong team concept does not automatically prove a best build, and a promising build does not prove a universal team.</p><h2>Where Runes and Karma fit</h2><p>Runes belong to the resource layer of a build, while Karma is listed here as a separate planning input whose exact effects and priorities remain unverified. Use the <a href="/systems/runes/">Runes page</a> for official 1.0.7 inventory and synthesis changes; do not infer a best set, drop rate or Karma recommendation from third-party guides.</p><h2>What we will verify next</h2><div class="card-grid"><GuideCard href="/characters/" title="Hero role" description="Identity and combat behavior, added only when verified."/><GuideCard href="/systems/runes/" title="Runes" description="Capacity and synthesis facts are current; optimal farming is not."/><GuideCard href="/teams/" title="Team order" description="Starter, connector and finisher logic without a fake tier list."/></div><AdsterraNativeBanner/><h2>Why there is no meta list yet</h2><p>Retail balance, unlock routes, exact skill interactions, Rune stats and Karma effects need direct play data. We will not publish an absolute best build, S-tier ranking, DPS ranking, fake skill priority, unsupported rotation or exact equipment recommendation.</p><AdsterraBanner300x250/></div><SourceList sources={sources}/></article></div></BaseLayout>
